1️⃣ What to Score

Your scoring system should cover two layers:

A. Metadata / SEO / Technical Quality

Title quality:

Length (50–70 chars ideal)

Keyword usage

Brand consistency

Meta description:

Length (150–160 chars ideal)

Unique vs duplicated

Presence of primary keyword

URL / handle:

Readable

Includes target keyword

Alt text on images:

Relevant

Present for every image

H1 / subheadings:

Proper structure

Includes relevant keywords

Structured data / schema (optional):

Product type, price, availability, rating

B. Content / UX Quality

Readability / clarity:

Use Flesch-Kincaid or similar scoring

Sentence length, paragraph length

Persuasiveness:

Mentions benefits over features

Includes social proof / trust signals

Consistency with brand voice:

Formal / casual / playful / technical

Can be AI-checked

Completeness:

Bullets, specifications, size/color info

SEO-friendliness:

Primary and secondary keyword usage

Keyword density, natural placement

Emotional engagement / storytelling:

Mentions problem → solution → benefit

Avoids common mistakes:

Typos

Repetition

Generic phrases like “best product ever”

2️⃣ How to Score

You can normalize all these into a 0–100 “QualiScore”, for example:

Category Weight Metrics inside Scoring method
Readability 20% Sentence/paragraph length, Flesch score AI + rules
SEO / Metadata 20% Title, meta, alt text, URL Rules + AI
Persuasiveness 20% Benefit-first copy, social proof AI semantic analysis
Completeness / Features 20% Bullet points, specs Rules
Brand voice & consistency 10% Tone, style AI comparison to brand template
Error-free / grammar 10% Typos, grammar AI grammar check
